BEGIN_PGML Find the difference [`-5.9-(-3.1)\text{.}`]
[_]{-2.8}{10}
END_PGML
########## # Solution ##########
BEGIN_PGML_SOLUTION We can rewrite this as [`-5.9+3.1\text{.}`] Now it is the sum of two numbers of opposite sign, so we find the difference [`5.9-3.1=2.8\text{.}`] We were adding two numbers where the larger one was negative. So the final result should also be negative: [`-2.8\text{.}`]
END_PGML_SOLUTION
